// Year 10 shipped at 0% short answer and 3% graphical. Real NAPLAN papers run
// 25-31% written-in answers — the 2013 Year 9 answer keys give 8 of 32 on the
// calculator paper and 10 of 32 on the non-calculator one — and carry a table or
// figure on nearly every page.
//
// Every question below carries a diagram and two thirds are short answer, which
// brings the level to roughly 40% graphical and 25% short answer. The diagram
// kinds follow what ACARA Year 10 covers: parabolas and linear models, bivariate
// and two-way data, comparing distributions, Pythagoras and trigonometry, and
// surds and inequalities on a number line.
