    format: 'extended_response',
    calculator_allowed: true,
    practice_set: 3,
    question_text: "An open cylindrical container has a circular base and a curved side, but no lid. It is to hold 500 cm³. The base has radius r cm and the container has height h cm.",
    parts: [
      { label: "a", prompt: "Show that h = 500/(πr²).", marks: 1, expected_answer: "πr²h = 500, so h = 500/(πr²)", explanation: "The volume of a cylinder is πr²h." },
      { label: "b", prompt: "Show that the total outside surface area of the container is S = πr² + 1000/r.", marks: 1, expected_answer: "S = πr² + 2πrh = πr² + 2πr × 500/(πr²) = πr² + 1000/r", explanation: "The base has area πr² and the curved side has area 2πrh." },
      { label: "c", prompt: "Find the value of r that minimises S. Give your answer correct to two decimal places.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "r ≈ 5.42 (exactly (500/π)^(1/3))", explanation: "dS/dr = 2πr − 1000/r² = 0 gives r³ = 500/π, so r ≈ 5.42. d²S/dr² = 2π + 2000/r³ > 0, confirming a minimum. One mark for the derivative equation, one for r." },
      { label: "d", prompt: "Find the minimum surface area, correct to the nearest square centimetre.", marks: 1, expected_answer: "277 cm²", explanation: "S(5.419…) ≈ 276.8, which is 277 cm² to the nearest square centimetre." },
      { label: "e", prompt: "Show that when S is a minimum, h = r.", marks: 1, expected_answer: "r³ = 500/π, so h = 500/(πr²) = r³/r² = r", explanation: "At the minimum πr³ = 500, so 500/(πr²) = πr³/(πr²) = r." },
      { label: "f", prompt: "The base material costs 0.05 cents per cm² and the side material costs 0.03 cents per cm². Find the radius that minimises the cost of a container, and the minimum cost. Give both answers correct to two decimal places.", marks: 3, expected_answer: "r ≈ 4.57 cm; minimum cost ≈ 9.85 cents", explanation: "Cost C = 0.05πr² + 0.03 × 1000/r = 0.05πr² + 30/r. dC/dr = 0.1πr − 30/r² = 0 gives r³ = 300/π, so r ≈ 4.57, and C ≈ 9.85 cents. One mark for the cost function, one for r, one for the cost." },
      { label: "g", prompt: "Only containers with 3 ≤ r ≤ 8 can be manufactured. Find the maximum cost of a container in this range, and the radius at which it occurs. Give the cost correct to two decimal places.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "13.80 cents, when r = 8", explanation: "C has a single stationary point (a minimum) in [3, 8], so the maximum is at an endpoint: C(3) ≈ 11.41 and C(8) ≈ 13.80. One mark for checking the endpoints, one for the answer." },
      { label: "h", prompt: "The container with minimum surface area from part c is filled with water at a constant rate of 25 cm³ per second. Find the rate at which the depth of the water is rising, in cm per second, correct to two decimal places.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "0.27 cm per second", explanation: "The volume of water at depth d is V = πr²d, with r fixed at about 5.419. dV/dt = πr² × dd/dt, so dd/dt = 25/(πr²) ≈ 25/92.26 ≈ 0.27. One mark for the relationship, one for the value." },
      { label: "i", prompt: "Find the average value of S for 3 ≤ r ≤ 8, correct to the nearest square centimetre.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "298 cm²", explanation: "Average value = (1/5)∫(πr² + 1000/r) dr from 3 to 8 = (1/5)[πr³/3 + 1000logₑ(r)] from 3 to 8 ≈ (1/5)(507.9 + 980.8) ≈ 297.7, which is 298 cm². One mark for the integral, one for the value." },
    ],
    explanation: "See the per-part marking guidance.",
    curriculum_code: 'VCE-MM-U34-AOS3',
